-- title:
--   Degree p of the forgetful degeneracy map when p ∣ M
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, let $M$ be a nonzero natural number, let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and let $p$ be a nonzero natural number dividing $M$; no primality of $p$ is assumed. Inside the Laurent series field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ consider two intermediate fields over $L$: the base change `laurentBaseChange L (xHFunctionField M H)`, that is the $L$-subfield generated by the image under `coeffEmb L` of the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionFieldC ℚ M H` of $\Gamma_H(M)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and the base change `laurentBaseChange L (xHTopFunctionFieldC ℚ M H (M * p))`, the $L$-subfield generated by the image of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CohCarrier.GammaH M H ⊓ CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 (M * p))`. The map [`ModularCurve.heckeAlphaHBar L M H p`](def/ModularCurve_XHHeckeOperator.html#L66) is the inclusion $L$-algebra homomorphism from the first into the second, induced by the inclusion of the underlying function fields over $\mathbb{Q}$. The assertion is that [`AlgebraicCurve.finrankAlong L`](def/AlgebraicCurve_Correspondence.html#L51) of this map, i.e. the $\mathrm{finrank}$ of the target as a module over the source via the algebra structure transported along the inclusion, equals $p$.
--
--   This is the degree of the forgetful degeneracy covering $X(\Gamma_H(M) \cap \Gamma_0(Mp)) \to X_H(M)$, read on function fields after base change to $L$: the source curve of the Hecke correspondence at an integer $p$ dividing the level has degree $p$ over $X_H(M)$. It is used in the companion degree computation for the second degeneracy map, in the Hecke operator and Atkin–Lehner relations on $X_H$, and in the construction of flat degeneracy charts in the reduction model at $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_finrankAlong_heckeAlphaHBar_of_dvd.lean

